  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale:\nOur approach integrates topology optimization with gradient-based learning to minimize the maximum overlap. The core idea is to iteratively refine a candidate solution by leveraging both global and local search strategies. We begin with a promising start provided by `initial_h_values` and apply coordinate-wise updates followed by projected gradient steps. The rationale is to balance exploration and exploitation by alternating between stochastic restarts and directed local minimization. This method addresses the curse of dimensionality inherent in the space-filling problem by focusing on local improvements while maintaining feasibility. The primary limitation is the potential for local minima, mitigated by multi-timescale random restarts. The hypothesis is that meaningful improvements can be achieved by leveraging the structure preserved in the initial solution.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification:\nWe represent the step function approximation as a sequence of n values, h[0..n-1] with:\n    - 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n    - \u2211_{i=0}^{n-1} h[i] * dx = 1   (dx = 2.0/n)\n\nThe objective is to compute the Voronoi overlap integral coefficient C5 defined by:\n    C5 = max_{k} (\u222b h(x) * (1 - h(x+k)) dx) * (n/2)   [scaled equivalent]\n\nWe define a mixed-integer programming constraint satisfaction approach where h[i] are continuous variables in [0,1] constrained by the integral condition. The gradient for coordinate descent is computed via:\n    \u2207_i C5 = max_k [ (1 - 2h[i+k]) * h[i] * (n/2) ] for appropriate k range\n\n3. Implementation Procedure:\n    Stage 0: Initialization\n        - Read seed and optionally existing initial_h_values\n        - Set initial_n = len(initial_h_values) if available else 300\n        - Define n_candidates = [300, 350, 500, 700] including original resolution\n        - Set time monitors to terminate after budget\n        - Initialize best_h and best_c with current best candidate\n\n    Stage 1: Local Refinement Loop\n        For n_dim in n_candidates:\n            if time exceeds budget after 10%: break\n            for each n_point in [350,500,700] including n_dim and a 2X supersampling version:\n                if calculation feasible and time > 0.5*budget: continue\n                Transform current best_h to new resolution via diffusion filtering\n                Apply coordinate-wise constrained optimization (saddle point seek)\n                Compute C5 with numpy correlate\n                Project to feasible set if required\n\n                Best update if lower C5 found\n\n    Stage 2: Multi-timescale Random Restarts\n        tsp = Traveling Salesman Problem over lag indices\n        n_restarts = 3 + min(5, 1100/300) scaled\n        For each restart:\n            Generate stochastic solution by Gaussian perturbation w/ scale sqrt(0.1/iters)\n            Use quadratic gradient to shield commonly good parameter ranges\n            Local coord descent until stability\n\n        Update global best at restart intervals\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations:\n    - Temperature evolution per randomized algorithm\n    - Lag space refinement: 4X oversampling of high-correlation regions\n    - Feature subset selection: retain top 90% coordinates by density\n    - Adaptive step scaling: learning rate annealing at 1, 5, 10 Hanke-Bregman restarts\n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness:\n    - Total iterations: 2000 max including restarts\n    - Wall time estimate: 900s for the core optimization loop\n    - Outlier detection: flag dimension subset when correlation exceeds 0.4\n    - Project via density projection ensuring \u2211h_i * dx = 1\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract:\n    At completion: \n        - Validate all h[?]: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1\n        - Verify \u2211_i h[i] * (2/n_points) = 1\n        - Recompute C5 with np.correlate and dx\n        - Output best_h, best_c, and n_points\n\nFallback on feasible solution if local search fails to converge, leveraging the original project_feasible mechanism.\n\nKey performance indicators: \n    - Best found: C5 improvement \u2265 0.95  \n    - Convergence metric: any stagnation for defined thresholds",
